---
/**
 * ReasonPanel — a `<dialog>` drawer with a REQUIRED reason textarea,
 * replacing `window.prompt()` for an action whose endpoint records a reason
 * (Issue #854 part 3, adapted from ahliweb/media-lenterakalteng's
 * `ReasonPanel.astro`, itself from its ADR-0123/0124 v2 shell work).
 *
 * ## Render this ONCE per page
 *
 * Like `#confirm-dialog`, this is ONE shared `<dialog>` instance, reused by
 * every opener button on the page — never one panel per row. Render it once
 * (commonly right before `</AdminLayout>`), then import `initReasonPanel`
 * from `../lib/ui/reason-panel-client` in the page's own `<script>` and call
 * it once.
 *
 * ## Wiring an opener — ZERO per-button JavaScript
 *
 * Mark any `<button type="button">` with the `data-reason-*` attributes
 * below. `initReasonPanel` finds every one of them (a delegated click
 * listener, the same pattern as `onAction` in `admin-form-client.ts`) — no
 * page-specific script is needed beyond the one `initReasonPanel()` call.
 *
 * | Attribute                 | Required | Default    | Meaning                                                                 |
 * | -------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
 * | `data-reason-title`       | yes      | —          | Panel heading.                                                          |
 * | `data-reason-description` | no       | (none)     | Note shown above the textarea (e.g. what this action does).            |
 * | `data-reason-action`      | one of this or `data-reason-form` | — | URL to send `{ [field]: reason }` to as JSON.                           |
 * | `data-reason-method`      | no       | `POST`     | HTTP method for `data-reason-action`.                                  |
 * | `data-reason-form`        | one of this or `data-reason-action` | — | `id` of an existing `<form>` on the page — the reason is written into a hidden field on it (named by `data-reason-field`) and the form is submitted normally. |
 * | `data-reason-field`       | no       | `reason`   | JSON body key (fetch mode) or hidden input `name` (form mode).         |
 * | `data-reason-min-length`  | no       | `1`        | Minimum trimmed characters before the submit button enables.           |
 * | `data-reason-max-length`  | no       | (none)     | Maximum characters — sets the textarea's native `maxlength` once this opener's config is active, so the browser itself stops further typing. |
 * | `data-reason-label`       | no       | panel's `defaultSubmitLabel` prop | This action's submit button text.                               |
 * | `data-reason-danger`      | no       | absent     | Presence (any value) styles the submit button as destructive.          |
 * | `data-reason-busy-label`  | no       | panel's `defaultBusyLabel` prop | Shown on the submit button while the request is in flight (fetch mode only). |
 * | `data-reason-failure`     | no       | panel's `defaultFailureMessage` prop | Shown in the panel if the request fails (fetch mode only).      |
 * | `data-reason-idempotent`  | no       | absent     | Fetch mode only. Presence (any value) sends an `Idempotency-Key: <uuid>` header alongside the JSON body — see `reason-panel-client.ts` for exactly when the key is (re)drawn. |
 *
 * ## Why `<dialog>`
 *
 * `showModal()` supplies the focus trap, the Escape handler, the page's
 * inertness behind it, the `::backdrop`, and focus restoration to the
 * opener — the same platform guarantees `ConfirmDialog` relies on.
 *
 * ## This is JavaScript-required, same as the `window.prompt()` it replaces
 *
 * Every opener this component replaces was already a
 * `<button type="button">` bound through a delegated click listener with no
 * `<form>` fallback — clicking it with JavaScript disabled already did
 * nothing. Swapping the confirmation surface from `window.prompt()` (JS-only)
 * to this dialog (also JS-only) is not a regression against that baseline, so
 * this component does not attempt to also work with JavaScript disabled —
 * unlike `SettingsSaveBar`, whose two buttons are the ONLY way some screens
 * submit their form at all.
 *
 * ## Props
 *
 * | Prop                    | Type     | Required | Notes                                                          |
 * | ------------------------ | -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------|
 * | `id`                    | `string` | no       | Dialog element id. Default `"admin-reason-panel"`.             |
 * | `cancelLabel`           | `string` | yes      | Cancel button text.                                             |
 * | `reasonLabel`           | `string` | yes      | Label above the textarea (e.g. `t("Reason")`).                 |
 * | `reasonHint`            | `string` | no       | Hint under the textarea.                                        |
 * | `defaultSubmitLabel`    | `string` | yes      | Fallback submit label when an opener omits `data-reason-label`.|
 * | `defaultBusyLabel`      | `string` | no       | Fallback busy label. Default `"Please wait…"`.                 |
 * | `defaultFailureMessage` | `string` | yes      | Fallback error text when an opener omits `data-reason-failure`.|
 *
 * ## Demo
 *
 * ```astro
 * <ReasonPanel
 *   cancelLabel={t("Cancel")}
 *   reasonLabel={t("Reason")}
 *   reasonHint={t("Recorded in the audit log.")}
 *   defaultSubmitLabel={t("Confirm")}
 *   defaultFailureMessage={t("Could not save this action. Please try again.")}
 * />
 *
 * <button
 *   type="button"
 *   class="btn-danger"
 *   data-reason-title={t('Disable module "{name}"', { name: mod.name })}
 *   data-reason-action={`/api/v1/tenant/modules/${mod.key}/disable`}
 *   data-reason-label={t("Disable")}
 *   data-reason-danger
 * >
 *   {t("Disable")}
 * </button>
 * ```
 */
interface Props {
  id?: string;
  cancelLabel: string;
  reasonLabel: string;
  reasonHint?: string;
  defaultSubmitLabel: string;
  defaultBusyLabel?: string;
  defaultFailureMessage: string;
}

const {
  id = "admin-reason-panel",
  cancelLabel,
  reasonLabel,
  reasonHint,
  defaultSubmitLabel,
  defaultBusyLabel = "Please wait…",
  defaultFailureMessage
} = Astro.props;
---

<dialog
  id={id}
  class="reason-panel"
  aria-labelledby={`${id}-title`}
  data-reason-panel
  data-default-submit-label={defaultSubmitLabel}
  data-default-busy-label={defaultBusyLabel}
  data-default-failure-message={defaultFailureMessage}
>
  <div class="reason-panel-header">
    <h2 class="reason-panel-title" id={`${id}-title`}></h2>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="reason-panel-close"
      data-reason-panel-close
      aria-label={cancelLabel}
    >
      <svg
        width="18"
        height="18"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="2"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
        focusable="false"
      >
        <path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"></path>
      </svg>
    </button>
  </div>
  <form method="dialog" class="reason-panel-body" data-reason-panel-form>
    <p
      class="reason-panel-description"
      data-reason-panel-description
      hidden
    ></p>
    <div class="reason-panel-field">
      <div class="reason-panel-label">
        {/* ahliweb/awcms#877 — this used to be a plain `<span>`: visually a
            label, but with no programmatic association to the textarea below
            it (axe: "Form elements must have labels", critical). A real
            `<label for>` fixes both the accessible name AND click-to-focus,
            which a `<span>` never had either. */}
        <label for={`${id}-textarea`}>
          {reasonLabel}
          <span class="reason-panel-required-marker" aria-hidden="true">
            {" "}
            *
          </span>
        </label>
        <span class="reason-panel-counter" data-reason-panel-counter></span>
      </div>
      <textarea
        class="reason-panel-textarea"
        id={`${id}-textarea`}
        rows="4"
        required
        aria-required="true"
        data-reason-panel-textarea
      ></textarea>
      {reasonHint !== undefined && (
        <p class="reason-panel-hint">{reasonHint}</p>
      )}
      <p
        class="reason-panel-error"
        role="alert"
        data-reason-panel-error
        hidden
      ></p>
    </div>
  </form>
  <div class="reason-panel-footer">
    <button type="button" class="btn-secondary" data-reason-panel-cancel>
      {cancelLabel}
    </button>
    <span class="reason-panel-spacer"></span>
    <button type="button" class="btn-primary" data-reason-panel-submit disabled>
      {defaultSubmitLabel}
    </button>
  </div>
</dialog>
